For the default parameters, `N = 128` fits in the 8-bit index. Assuming reset initializes the module, these lemmas strengthen `prop` into a 1-inductive invariant. Concurrent assertions sample the state before updates at the clock edge. ([accellera.org](https://www.accellera.org/images/resources/videos/SystemVerilog_Assertions_Tutorial_2016.pdf?utm_source=openai))

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (i <= N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The index starts at zero and increments only while below N. This bound excludes unreachable overrange LOOP states from the induction step."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) ((state != DONE) || (i >= N)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The FSM enters DONE only when the index is at least N. Together with lemma_1, this establishes i == N in DONE."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (sum == (i / 8)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The sum increments precisely when the updated index reaches a multiple of eight. The index bound prevents wraparound, so in DONE, sum == N / 8 == n."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

For the default parameters, `i` reaches `N = 128`, `sum` increments at each multiple of eight, and the next step enters `DONE`. The assertions observe values sampled before the current clock-edge updates. ([accellera.org](https://www.accellera.org/images/eda/sv-bc/att-0517/01-schedSem-svLRM-v6.pdf)) These lemmas are **jointly 1-inductive**, assuming reset occurs and `N` fits in `i`; if `i` wraps, the count relationship need not hold.

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (i <= N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Reset sets i to zero, and LOOP increments it only while i < N. This excludes unreachable induction states beyond the terminal count."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (sum == i / 8); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The divisibility test uses the incremented i, so sum increases precisely when i reaches 8, 16, and subsequent multiples of eight."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (state != DONE || i == N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "LOOP enters DONE only when i >= N; lemma_1 makes this i == N. Lemma_2 then gives sum == N / 8 == n, proving the target."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

For the default parameters, these lemmas jointly make `prop` 1-inductive **after reset**. The blocking assignment increments `i` before the divisibility check, so `sum` counts completed groups of eight. Concurrent assertions evaluate sampled values at the clock edge. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf))

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (i <= N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Bounds the loop index. Once it reaches N, the LOOP state stops incrementing it."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (state == DONE) |-> (i == N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Together with the index bound, establishes that the transition to DONE occurs only at the terminal index."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (sum == (i / 8)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Captures the counter invariant: each completed group of eight increments sum once. At DONE, i equals N = 8*n, so sum equals n."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

These lemmas assume `N` fits in `i`; that holds for `WIDTH=8, n=16`. The final increment also attempts to write `a[N]`, outside the array’s `0` through `N-1` indices. That write is a separate RTL issue and is not needed to prove this counter property.

For the default parameters, `N = 128` fits in the 8-bit `i`. Assuming reset establishes the initial state, the following invariants jointly make `prop` 1-inductive. They rely on `N` being nonnegative and representable by `i`; otherwise the counter can wrap. Concurrent assertions sample state before the clock-edge updates. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf))

