  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (i <= N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The index starts at zero, increments only while below N, and stops at N. This bound rules out an out-of-range index when LOOP transitions to DONE."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (sum == (i >> 3)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The modulo test sees the incremented i, so sum increases exactly when i reaches another multiple of eight. The bound in lemma_1 prevents wraparound from breaking this relationship."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) ((state != DONE) || (i == N)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "LOOP exits only when i is at least N; lemma_1 makes it exactly N. Thus, in DONE, lemma_2 gives sum = N / 8 = n."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

The blocking assignment increments `i` before the divisibility test, so `sum` counts multiples of eight reached by `i`. The lemmas below use that relationship and assume the formal run establishes reset before checking the property. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf))

